('127.263.d.8.B',4,'Lowering operating expenses by saving on utilities can allow:','["Higher rent", "More flexibility in pricing", "Less profit by law", "Fewer customers"]'::jsonb,1,'Costs affect price room.','original'),
('127.263.d.8.C',3,'Setting a price based on what rivals charge is:','["Cost-plus pricing", "Free pricing", "Competition-based pricing", "Demand-based pricing"]'::jsonb,2,'Follows competitors.','original'),
('127.263.d.8.C',4,'Raising prices on umbrellas during a storm is an example of:','["Cost-based pricing", "Loss leading", "Competition-based pricing", "Demand-based pricing"]'::jsonb,3,'Demand lifts price.','original'),
('127.263.d.8.D',3,'A retailer with a large market share often has:','["More power to influence prices", "No power", "Higher costs always", "Fewer customers"]'::jsonb,0,'Share gives leverage.','original'),
('127.263.d.8.D',4,'A small shop in a market dominated by a giant retailer usually has to:','["Stop selling", "Compete on service or niche rather than price", "Hide products", "Match every price"]'::jsonb,1,'Differentiation.','original'),
('127.263.d.8.E',3,'Keystone pricing means a retailer sets the retail price at:','["The cost", "Cost plus 5%", "Double the cost", "Half the cost"]'::jsonb,2,'Keystone = 100% markup.','original'),
('127.263.d.8.E',4,'An item costs a store $18. Its keystone price is:','["$9", "$18", "$27", "$36"]'::jsonb,3,'18 x 2.','original'),
('127.263.d.9.A',3,'The six elements of communication include source, message, channel, receiver, feedback, and:','["Noise", "Product", "Price", "Profit"]'::jsonb,0,'Interference.','original'),
